   "source": [
    "## conclusion\n",
    "\n",
    "Random Forest wins on RMSE (1143 vs 1331) and R2 (0.48 vs 0.30), MAE is close either way. R2 of 0.48 means the model explains under half the day to day variance, which is just aight, theres clearly other stuff going on like local events, random day to day noise that these features dont capture. basically external factors that need to be taking into account\n",
    "\n",
    "Biggest predictors are yr (basically capturing overall growth from 2011 to 2012) and temp (warmer means more rentals, up to a point). Season and weathersit matter too but less than those two\n",
    "\n",
    "The test period (last 60 days) happens to be in late fall/winter, so this doesnt really tell how good the model is at predicting the busy summer season. a proper evaluation wouldve tested on a few different time windows across different seasons instead of just one. maybe i need to change that lol\n",
    "\n",
    "But, for an actual bike share company even a moderate model like this could help with fleet sizing or staffing, knowing a warm day needs way more bikes available than a cold one is a useful signal even if the exact number isnt perfect"
   ]
